{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/458868-other-fiction-as-werewolves","id":458868,"title":"Other Fiction as Werewolves.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-27T05:46:58-07:00","id":458868,"title":"Other Fiction as Werewolves.","content":"Similar to a thread on the Vampire forum and the Changeling forum, I thought we'd do a little genre mashing. Pick a book, show, story, whatever, and make it werewolf. I'll start with a few of my current favorites. I'm going to eschew Tribes and concentrate on Auspices, unless it's ridiculously obvious.<br /> <br /> <b>House of Lies</b><br /> <br /> Marty Kaan, <i>Elodoth</i>; the mastermind alpha behind it all, coordinating his pack with precision and stifling catastrophies left and right, his sense of honor is deeply tied to loyalty to his family and pack; woe to any who drive him to financial Death Rage.<br /> <br /> Jeannie Van Der Hooven, <i>Irraka</i>; the beta, sneaky and all around duplicitous, but not without deep love for her pack when the chips are down. She's been known to cross them at stressful times, but one wonders if that's not her role in the group.<br /> <br /> Clyde Oberholt, <i>Cahalith</i>; loud and proud, Clyde is always telling stories, yelling, cursing. He's the emotional outlet for the group: when no one wants to say something, it's Clyde that shouts it in their faces, just to make it clear that it exists.<br /> <br /> Doug Guggenheim, <i>Ithaeur</i>; the omega, fucking creepy and all-around greedy like a motherfucker, Doug the Gug's ability to mess around with spirits, especially those of finance and money is unaparalleled. He may be a selfish, dishonest creeper, but he's the pack's selfish, dishonest creeper.<br /> <br /> Last but not least,<br /> <br /> Monica Talbot, <i>Rahu</i>; man, this bitch is cray. And she's Marty's ex. She's on the outs with the pack now, but she used to be their top enforcer, always ready to lay it all on the line and go into battle screaming with lunacy in her veins and blood on her teeth.<br /> <br /> <b>Banshee</b><br /> <br /> Hood, <i>Rahu</i>; the alpha of the pack, and so angry inside he makes the Hulk seem kind of chill. His solution to just about everything is to throw down, and he does it extremely well. Once he's set his sights on something, dragging him down is an exercise in futility.<br /> <br /> Job, <i>Ithaeur</i>; the beta of the pack, Job tries to keep everyone on task all the time. It doesn't always work. But he's amazing with spirits, to the point where his name is his legend, and he made himself and Hood disappear from society years ago, giving them absolute fresh starts.<br /> <br /> Carrie, <i>Irraka</i>; so sneaky, this one, able to infiltrate lives and create them wholesale, to the point where she lived a whole nother life with someone else, until the Hunt came calling to her again. She fights pragmatically and puts down her enemies efficiently, using their prejudices against them.<br /> <br /> Sugar, <i>Cahalith</i>; quite older than the others and past his prime, don't let it fool you when it comes time to <i>throw down</i>. Sugar still packs a mean bite. He owns the bar, and everything's a moral tale or a story to him, even though his own morals are compromised half the time and he uses booze to help him cope with that.<br /> <br /> Last but not least,<br /> <br /> Gordon, <i>Elodoth</i>; on the outs with the pack, even his wife, Carrie, Gordon continually attempts to make them go legit, even though they're much more apt at bringing him down to their level than he is in getting them to step up their game. Gordon likes rules and laws, but he's learning they don't need to be <i>human</i> rules and laws...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3855,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","user":"gebbethine","date":". 03-27-2015, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}